000000) - (1001)(2000000)\n\\]\n\nWe can factor out the common term \\(2000000\\):\n\n\\[\n2000000 \\left(1001001 - 1001\\right)\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify the term inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n1001001 - 1001 = 1000000\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n2000000 \\times 1000000 = 2 \\times 10^6 \\times 10^6 = 2 \\times 10^{12}\n\\]\n\nThe number \\(2 \\times 10^{12}\\) has the rightmost non-zero digit \\(2\\) and is followed by \\(12\\) zeroes. Therefore, the ordered pair \\((a, b)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{(2, 12)}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{(2, 12)}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
